# Boolean fit checks — never printed or sliced, rendered by gate.sh.
# Each part name must match a `part == "<name>"` dispatch branch in the
# entry .scad — that is the branch gate.sh renders.
#
# fitcheck-slot: the peg's blade (web + hammer heads) seated in the E2020
#   slot as installed — neck through the 6.0 mouth with slot_fit_tol per
#   side, heads hooking the 2.0 lips inside the 12.0 cavity, plate on the
#   face. Zero facets = the peg slides in clean.
# fitcheck-slot-ctrl: the same assembly with slot_fit_tol = -0.15, so the
#   neck (6.3) is wider than the mouth (6.0) — real overlap. The mandatory
#   negative control: if this ever renders empty, the slot check above is
#   proving nothing.
# fitcheck-bore: the spool bore (a tube swept by the bore surface,
#   max-width 71 mm spool) seated on the shoulder — zero facets = the
#   spool drops on and spins at bore_clearance.
# fitcheck-bore-ctrl: the same tube 0.2 undersized — the stub must
#   overlap it.
fitcheck-slot       empty
fitcheck-slot-ctrl  interferes
fitcheck-bore       empty
fitcheck-bore-ctrl  interferes
